      "claim": "The performance configuration table misleadingly permits workspace or environment values up to the listed hard maxima even when those values exceed built-in defaults.",
      "basis": "The documentation explicitly says workspace and environment values may only lower built-in defaults, while governed requirements separately distinguish safe defaults from immutable maxima [qa-v1-block-9a637580a721b349e21044c1, qa-v1-block-ce45392d2ebc036986b89d13].",
      "verification_surface": "Compare the documented configuration semantics and limits table with typed validation in internal/platform/config/performance.go.",
      "expectation_refs": [
        "contract-configuration",
        "contract-documentation",
        "contract-performance"
      ],
      "severity_if_confirmed": "medium",
      "confirmation_condition": "Configuration validation accepts values above defaults up to the documented hard maxima, contradicting the lower-only requirement, or documentation states that operators may configure those larger values.",
      "refutation_condition": "Configuration validation rejects every value above its built-in default, while larger hard maxima are only immutable product ceilings and documentation explicitly states that configuration may only lower defaults.",
      "inconclusive_condition": "The effective configuration validator or intended meaning of the hard-maximum column cannot be inspected.",
      "safe_evidence_strategy": "Read only typed performance configuration defaults and validation logic; do not execute commands or modify configuration.",
